Package: torchgnn
Title: Graph Neural Networks for 'torch'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Josiah", "Parry", , "josiah.parry@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9910-865X"))
Description: Build and train graph neural networks on top of the 'torch'
    deep learning framework. Message-passing layers are provided for the
    Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) of Kipf and Welling (2017)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1609.02907>, the GraphSAGE architecture of Hamilton,
    Ying and Leskovec (2017) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1706.02216>, the Graph
    Attention Network (GAT) of Velickovic and others (2018)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1710.10903>, the Graph Isomorphism Network (GIN) of
    Xu and others (2019) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1810.00826>, and the regional
    GCN of Guo and others (2025) <doi:10.1080/24694452.2025.2558661>. These
    layers are composed into ready-made node-level and graph-level models.
    Supporting utilities construct sparse adjacency matrices from edge
    lists, normalize them, pool node embeddings into graph-level
    representations, and split graphs into training, validation and test
    sets.
